Machine Exercise 3
Student: Kent Justin Canja


The aim is to build a full-duplex, voice-enabled AI agent running on a Raspberry Pi (4 or 5). 
Your responsibilities:

* Install AI agent harness (e.g. onit, pipecat, crew) with MCP support on RPi
* Build MCP servers that to SOTA ASR and TTS
* Install VAD on RPi for voice detection,
* Run a full-duplex AI agent that can real-world tasks
* You may use commercial APIs for models but you build and run your MCP servers (on RPi)
* Build a latency benchmark (classwork): a standardized latency measurement method. Note that this is . Speech interaction is natural, conversational and interruptible.